Package: plurx-player
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.10), zenity
# M5: the private build replaces this; until then the system mpv is used.
Recommends: mpv
Description: Dolby Vision playback of plurx titles on Linux
 plurx Player plays titles handed over from the plurx web app ("Open titles
 in: plurx Player") in mpv, keeping the original Dolby Vision stream for
 profile 5 and 8 titles and receiving profile 7 FEL titles as profile 8.1.
 .
 HDR output needs a Wayland compositor with wp_color_manager_v1 in HDR mode,
 such as GNOME in HDR mode. An accurate target luminance needs a compositor
 that reports the panel's real luminance; stock compositors may report a
 default instead.
